{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011Cd4xcooQeDxqkMKSqBH6C","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 6 scenarios pass — the 2 new limit scenarios plus the 4 original reservation scenarios that had to stay green. (The Korean text in the Maven output is garbled by the Windows console encoding, but the results line is unambiguous.)\n\nHere's what I added:\n\n**`TicketLimitExceededException`** — the new exception named in the requirements, matching the style of the existing ones.\n\n**`Buyer`** — a small domain class that knows the limit rule. The existing code had already established this pattern: `Ticket` wraps `TicketRecord` and answers \"can this be reserved?\" via `requireReservable()`. `Buyer` wraps `UserRecord` plus the count from the new `countByUserId`, and answers \"can this member hold one more?\" the same way. That kept `TicketService` a thin orchestrator instead of growing an inline `if` for each new rule.\n\n**`TicketService.reserveTicket`** — two lines, placed after the member lookup and before the ticket lookup:\n\n```java\nBuyer buyer = Buyer.of(user, tickets.countByUserId(userId));\nbuyer.requireCanHoldOneMore();\n```\n\nThe placement is what satisfies the \"청구는 일어나지 않는다\" part of the requirement. Every rejection reason is still decided before `payments.charge` is reached, so a member who already holds a ticket is turned away without any charge attempt — which is exactly what the `결제는 청구되지 않는다` step asserts.\n\nI didn't touch `provided`, `src/test/`, or `pom.xml`, and the contract's entry point and constructor are unchanged, as `change-ticket-limit.md` specified.\n\nOne thing worth flagging: `Buyer` reads the held-ticket count once at construction. That's fine within the stated scope — `spec.md` explicitly puts concurrent reservation races out of scope — but if two requests for the same member ever ran concurrently, both could pass the check before either saved. That would need the store to enforce it, and the store is off-limits here."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2606,"cache_read_input_tokens":40131,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2606},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"009ebef5-3d35-48ae-908c-baed987112d1","uuid":"711815ed-eac7-4935-bd3b-a5fce34a6a19","timestamp":"2026-07-16T02:37:49.676Z","request_id":"req_011Cd4xcn3zAnMvqJXWBeF3o"}
